mouse-hover

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Report pointer motion without a pressed button to programs that enable any-event mouse tracking (mode 1003), as Ghostty does, so hover reaches TUIs; the encoder filters by mode, and motion within one cell is dropped except in SGR-pixels mode.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream herdr-app forwards buttonless motion to the mouse encoder.
---
 src/terminal.rs |    4 +++-
 src/vt.rs       |   27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/terminal.rs b/src/terminal.rs
index ec5a6c5c188c493f34ee650763f218f6ce6cbfca..a0ba4b41a12daa0f7d4d2914b672143c03306322 100644
--- a/src/terminal.rs
+++ b/src/terminal.rs
@@ -1273,7 +1273,9 @@ impl Render for TerminalView {
                 }
                 if this.selecting && ev.pressed_button == Some(MouseButton::Left) {
                     this.select(Select::Drag, ev.position, cx);
-                } else if this.grid.borrow().buttons_down > 0 {
+                } else {
+                    // The encoder reports motion only as the program's mode asks
+                    // (1002 with a button down, 1003 always), once per cell.
                     this.mouse(GHOSTTY_MOUSE_ACTION_MOTION, ev.pressed_button, ev.position, ev.modifiers);
                 }
             }))
